for 39 years a las vegas woman named  vicki tatum has been waiting for her  husband to return home from work vince  tatum was a corrections officer sergeant  at the state prison near indian springs  and was investigating possible criminal  activity by fellow officers now metro  cold case detectives have the names of  the main suspects but they need help in  resolving this mystery the i-team's  george knapp has our story  he was a family man vicki tatum and her  husband vince had been married for only  two years when he vanished that was 39  years ago but she's never given up hope  of finding out who killed them i can't  even describe how terrible an awful that  is to be waiting for someone who never  comes home vince tatum was a decorated  corrections officer a sergeant at  southern desert correctional a state  prison near indian springs he had  undertaken a quiet investigation into  criminal activity at the prison the  possibility that fellow officers might  be involved in smuggling drugs and guns  to inmates and or a theft and  embezzlement ring he never told his wife  the details but hinted that something  was amiss shortly before he disappeared  he had brought home a gun it was a  prison issue gun and he told me how to  shoot it and he says if i'm not here  something happens this way you can  protect yourself at one am august 31st  1982 tatum finished his shift at the  prison drove toward las vegas and  dropped off a fellow officer donna smith  he said he was going to a confidential  meeting nearly a month later his body  was found in a shallow grave near what  is now a neighborhood at sunrise  mountain not far from the tatum home  he'd been shot five times in the head  with a 25 caliber weapon  weeks after that tatum's vehicle was  found at the railroad pass casino police  suspicions focused on fellow officers  including corrections lieutenant lovell  gaines at the time the president of the  local naacp and officer clyde johnson as  well as donna smith metro questioned all  three multiple times and they were  placed on extended leave gaines who had  been to the tatum home for dinner  clammed up and declined to turn over a  handgun he owned for testing a 25  caliber i know there are limits on what  you can say but those names obviously  appear in that file somewhere don't they  sure yes they were interviewed  every one of them cold case homicide  detective dan long was given this thick  file a year ago in response to a plea  from vicki tatum to finally solve the  case he says the original detectives did  a commendable job and it zeroed in on  the same three names gaines johnson and  smith but could never get enough to take  it further both gaines and johnson were  suspects and other serious allegations  at the time but those charges didn't  stick he does not believe donna smith  was knowingly involved in the murder the  good thing is that the suspects that we  suspect killed  him are dead  so the threat level is it's much lower  both level gains and clyde johnson died  years ago johnson reportedly made a  deathbed confession but police can't  prove it if you do know something  like i said we can solve this case  and  and  give the family some peace i feel like  i've been waiting almost 40 years  i feel like that prison at least owes me  an explanation  george knapp 8 news now
 

